Each to his own. But mine is like this.

The source trees:

--- nethack-3.4.3 --- official --- src
|                |            |
|                |            --- include
|                |            |
|                |            --- etc.
|                |
|                --- AoY --- etc.
|                |
|                --- Artifact --- etc.
|                |
|                --- etc.
|
--- nethack-3.4.2 --- etc.
|
--- etc.

Then if I'm making changes to the amulet in container patch I work in 
the AoY tree and finally give the diff command on that root directory:

diff -bruNX ignore.txt . ../official >aoycont.diff

I use local ignore-files as my directories might have several files that 
are not part of the patch release. Every time I start a new project I 
copy a sceleton ignore.txt and I always read the resulting diff-file so 
I can see if there is any garbage in it. If there is I remedy the 
situation by editing the ignore.txt-file.

Those switches are -b ignore space changes, -r recursively compare any 
subdirectories found, -u unified diff, -N treat absent files as empty, 
-X FILE exclude any files that match a pattern in FILE (in my case 
ignore.txt)

